Thus perhaps the goal does not require origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded; the establish clearance actions may not require those flags? Wait they do: establish_clearance_origin_loaded requires origin_leg_loaded true, destination_leg_loaded false. establish_clearance_destination_loaded requires origin_leg_loaded false, destination_leg_loaded true. establish_clearance_full_load requires both true.

Thus to get candidate_clearance_established we need one of those three. Since goal requires candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta, we need to satisfy one of those. But goal also requires origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed true (as separate goals). So we need to have both confirmed and also have either origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded (or both) true. However the assemble actions that set leg loaded require the opposite confirmation status. So we cannot have both confirmed and leg loaded simultaneously.

